  "summary": "The audit checks a statistics course, COMM 1, 106 and 108, four area courses with at least one from each area, a WIM course (it can also be one of the area courses), a capstone, and 65 units in all, made up with any COMM electives plus up to 10 units from the pre-approved list in other departments. Every course needs a C- or better, and every COMM course a letter grade unless it is only offered S/NC. You check by hand the 2.0 GPA in major courses, petitioned courses, and for honors the 3.3 GPA in COMM courses, the application and the faculty recommendation.",
